Security: Prevent user enumeration via the login form

The login form derived the visibility of the "Reset it?" link from the user
backend's canChangePassword() capability, which made the response for an
existing account differ from the response for a non-existing one. The
capability check has been removed; the link is shown uniformly.

Unlike upstream, the submitted login name is echoed back verbatim and is
never resolved against the user backend, because resolving it would echo the
canonical spelling for existing accounts only and thereby reintroduce the
enumeration oracle on an unthrottled GET request.

